{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
  "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Gregory S. Coleman",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Racial classifications are inherently pernicious and, if not checked, lead as they did in New Haven to regrettable and socially destructive racial politics."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem, Mr. Coleman, is that -- that the cases you are relying on, it seems to me, are cases in which ultimately what is being judged is a different result in the -- at the end point of the process which was starting."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Coleman",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All we're asking for is that the City undertake an honest and -- and open assessment of are we really likely to be liable here under the disparate impact provision of Title VII."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has long recognized that Title VII prohibits not only intentional discrimination but acts that are discriminatory in their operation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The disparate impact test has been recognized since Griggs as fundamental to fulfilling the purposes of Title VII."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What do you think of an employer who does the following? He advertises a job. Everyone comes in and applies. He says May 1 is the deadline. When he sees the applicants, he thinks, I'd prefer more diversity. And solely because he lacks diversity among women, minorities, and whatever, he says, you know, I'm going to extend the deadline 2 months, and I hope I'll get a few more minority or female applicants."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the government consider promotion of diversity by itself a compelling state interest in the employment context as opposed to the school context?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents (Mr. Kneedler)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think -- we think it probably is a compelling state interest, but it is not one that -- that can be advanced by race -- by racial classifications. And that -- and that is our basic submission here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And then -- and you want us to say this isn't race? I have -- I have trouble with this argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents (Mr. Meade)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Employers, both private and public, are required to comply with Title VII's disparate impact provisions, which seek to root out barriers to equal opportunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If all the employer has is evidence that the test results violate the four-fifths rule, is that sufficient?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't see how you can call it facially neutral."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What has New Haven done in fact?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: When you say \"take away barriers,\" one thing is not a hundred percent clear. Your position is we have to do this in order to avoid Title VII disparate impact liability. Are you not reciting as a justification either the diversity in police -- policing firefighting or still overcoming a"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "City",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MEADE: We're not saying that. We did not say that below. And, in fact, the board members who voted against certification cited flaws with the test and flaws with the process, and that was the basis for their failure to certify."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the board heard 5 days of testimony over 2 months."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0003-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A court will often need to use racial quotas or set-asides to try to undo or to remedy the discrimination that has happened."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What difference does the cut-off score make?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Human Resources Professionals",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0003-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "scores. And the amicus brief of the human resources -- human resources professionals points out this point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if it were shown that, in fact, this test was not job-related and, in fact, the majority of fire departments scotched this test years ago and substituted what most agree is a better test, even so you would say it would violate the rights of the plaintiffs you represent, even --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Even if there's strong evidence that it's not job-related and that there's a better test that doesn't produce these skewed results?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But in your -- in my example, to go back, the thing you've identified, it seems to me, is Texas couldn't do this. It couldn't look at the class that they're going to choose with the 10 percent and say, you know, there are not enough minorities, I think we'll go to 15 percent this year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You are -- you are saying, as I understand it, that if the -- if the city in a case like this, prior to giving a test, looked at the test and says, wait a minute, this is going to produce really disparate results, they can stop, regroup, and think it through again and maybe come up with a different test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0004-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if they see it coming, they don't have to show a strong basis in evidence for changing the test prior to the time they give it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1428",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1ed1f7d6b30f1720b7dd5a27f67a8652abb406b393a658570ec1bde2651484a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1ed1f7d6b30-0004-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:33 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
